  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c0e89f31",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Feature Engeneering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "b0af47fa",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data[\"Avg_spent_per_flight\"] = np.where(data[\"EnrollmentDateOpening\"] >= \"2019-01-01\",\n",
    "                                        data[\"Customer Lifetime Value\"]/(data[\"Flights_per_day\"] * data[\"Days_in_prog\"]),\n",
    "                                        np.nan)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7b6dd5d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\"Inf\" means infinity, which happens when the divisor is zero, so when \"Days_in_prog\" or \"Flights_per_day\" is zero. To handle this, we will feel it with Nan for now."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "a506f00a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data[\"Avg_spent_per_flight\"] = data[\"Avg_spent_per_flight\"].replace(np.inf, np.nan)"
   ]
  },
